        "modalSubtitle": "Decompression, fusion and motion-preserving disc replacement",
        "modalContent": "### Diseases of the cervical spine\nChanges in the cervical spine can affect nerve roots and, in certain cases, the spinal cord. Possible complaints range from neck and arm pain to numbness, reduced strength or fine motor problems.\n\n### Which operation is suitable?\nDepending on the diagnosis, different procedures may be useful, including decompression, fusion or, in selected cases, a motion-preserving disc replacement.\n\nA disc prosthesis is not suitable for every patient. Whether a prosthesis makes sense depends, among other things, on the affected segment, the extent of degenerative changes, stability, bone quality and other individual factors. The recommendation is only made after examination and image evaluation.",
