        "modalSubtitle": "Cubital tunnel syndrome and other entrapment syndromes",
        "modalContent": "### Nerve compression – what happens?\nPeripheral nerves can come under pressure at various anatomical constrictions. This leads to impaired nerve function, which can manifest as tingling, numbness, pain or reduced strength.\n\nThe symptoms are often intermittent at first and worsen with certain postures or stress. If the damage is prolonged or more severe, failures can become permanent.\n\n### Diagnosis and treatment\nThe diagnosis is confirmed through clinical examination and – if necessary – through electrophysiological measurements (nerve conduction velocity, EMG). Imaging can be used additionally.\n\nWhether conservative or surgical treatment is indicated depends on the symptoms, the clinical findings, the extent of the nerve damage and the cause of the compression.",
