        "modalContent": "### Complex and Chronic Pain Syndromes\nChronic pain can have very diverse causes and significantly impair quality of life. As specialized neurosurgical pain therapists, we focus particularly on complex and chronic pain syndromes of the nervous system, spine, and musculoskeletal system.\n\nThese include neuropathic pain, phantom limb pain, and chronic postoperative and post-interventional pain syndromes. Even with persistent pain following spinal surgery or other interventions, we perform targeted diagnostics and therapy planning.\n\n### Individualized &amp; Multimodal Therapy Planning\nFollowing comprehensive diagnostics, we develop a personalized treatment concept. Depending on the underlying cause, pharmacological, physical, physiotherapeutic, psychosomatic, and interventional procedures may be combined. For selected patients, modern neuromodulation techniques are also considered.\n\n### Holistic Approach – Outpatient and Inpatient\nDepending on the nature and severity of the symptoms, treatment can be carried out on an outpatient basis. For complex chronic pain syndromes, multimodal inpatient pain therapy may also be appropriate where medically indicated.\n\nOur goal is not merely treating isolated symptoms. We consider physical, neurological, and psychosomatic factors together to formulate the most effective and tailored therapy.",
